  DNA v64/v65 -- DOES THE RHYTHM TRACK THE JAW?
  NOTE THE SCOPE: target_amp = jaw_, so tracking shows the mechanism
  works as built, not that the creature gained a usable frame.
    jaw_hz 3.0  ->  envelope peak 3.04 +/- 0.23 Hz   snr 14.3   amp 0.3113
    jaw_hz 4.5  ->  envelope peak 4.24 +/- 0.25 Hz   snr 7.5   amp 0.3067
    jaw_hz 7.0  ->  envelope peak 6.46 +/- 0.73 Hz   snr 7.6   amp 0.2981
    TRACKING SLOPE 0.86  [1.00 is the jaw; 0.00 is a fixed resonance]
    mean |peak - jaw_hz| 0.28 Hz
    mean amplitude, jaw 4.5 0.3067 vs no jaw 0.2998 (a mute dial would fall)
    modulation depth, jaw 4.5 0.4889 vs no jaw 0.3624

    THE MECHANISM WORKS AS BUILT. The envelope peak tracks jaw_hz at
    slope 0.86 without the voice going quiet, where v64's damped spring
    managed 0.01 -- a limit cycle can impose a frequency and a resonator
    structurally cannot.
    BUT READ IT NARROWLY: an oscillator is wired to the amplitude output,
    so the envelope following it is nearly a definition. What is NOT shown
    is that the creature gained a usable frame.
    The slope being 0.86 rather than 1.00 is the informative part: the jaw
    is coupled to the drive through w0^2*(x - drive), so a drive with
    energy near 2.5-3 Hz ENTRAINS it and the peak is a compromise between
    the body's rate and the brain's. That is frames-then-content with the
    brain able to influence timing.
    NEXT: a fresh seed family, and whether reward can shape what the body
    supplies -- `jaw4.5+rew` begins it and full power would settle it.

  SCALE-INVARIANT SALIENCE, against its OWN yoked control
    modulation depth  +0.0150 +/- 0.0058  (+2.6 SE)   <- THE PRIMARY
    mean amplitude    -0.0058 +/- 0.0030  (-1.9 SE)   <- the loophole
    for comparison, the ABSOLUTE reward moved mod -0.0091 and amp +0.0104
    against the unrewarded jaw.

    REFUSED AT THE BAR, BUT THE FIX CHANGED THE SIGN OF BOTH CHANNELS.
    Modulation +2.6 SE (3.0 required) so the pre-registered bar is not
    cleared -- and the absolute reward moved modulation -0.0091 with
    amplitude +0.0104 where the normalised one moves +0.0150 and -0.0058. Volume
    WAS part of what stood between the reward and the rhythm. This is
    UNDERPOWERED rather than null: 1.32x the creatures reaches 3.0, i.e.
    16 instead of 12. Do not write it up as a refusal of the mechanism.

  --- the reading ---
  REFUSED, AND ON THE ARM THAT CAN CARRY IT. With the bar FIXED the reward
  fired on 49.0% of windows all run, and syllable-band modulation depth
  still does not beat yoked praise (+1.6 SE; the ratcheting arm +0.1 SE).
  So it is not that the reward stopped arriving -- it arrived continuously
  and did not build a frame. Warlaumont's reward is NOT refuted: what is
  refused is that it installs a frame in THIS larynx, which has no jaw and,
  per `no-sequence`, no module that holds a kick for 10 ms. Their
  oscillation comes from a 1000-neuron recurrent reservoir; this vocal
  module is 126 neurons in 9 groups.
